{"name":"Felt","hex":"#247345","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Felt","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Felt"}],"entries":[{"title":"Felt","blocks":[{"text":"Felt is a textile that is produced by matting, condensing, and pressing fibers together. Felt can be made of natural fibers such as wool or animal fur, or from synthetic fibers such as petroleum-based acrylic or acrylonitrile or wood pulp–based rayon. Blended fibers are also common. Natural fiber felt has special properties that allow it to be used for a wide variety of purposes. It is \"fire-retardant and self-extinguishing; it dampens vibration and absorbs sound; and it can hold large amounts of fluid without feeling wet...\""}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Colored_felt_cloth.jpg/330px-Colored_felt_cloth.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Felt"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Kazah_jurta.jpg/500px-Kazah_jurta.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Kazah_jurta.jpg/500px-Kazah_jurta.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Kazakh felt yurt","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKazah_jurta.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/A_Hawrami_man_with_traditional_headdress%2C_Kurdistan.jpg/500px-A_Hawrami_man_with_traditional_headdress%2C_Kurdistan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/A_Hawrami_man_with_traditional_headdress%2C_Kurdistan.jpg/500px-A_Hawrami_man_with_traditional_headdress%2C_Kurdistan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnai